or vehicle traffic on all publicly maintained highways, covering both centrally and locally managed roads.  While road traffic estimates are robust at higher levels of aggregation, local authority splits and temporal distributions are less robust, reflecting limitations in sample size and coverage. These datasets are therefore labelled as Official Statistics to reflect this.  Further information on definitions and methodology, along with information on data quality and robustness, is available in the [Department for Transport Background Quality Report](https://www.gov.uk/government/statistics/road-traffic-estimates-in-great-britain-2024/background-quality-report).  Department for Transport also publish [road length statistics by local authority](https://www.gov.uk/government/statistical-data-sets/road-length-statistics-rdl#road-length-in-miles-rdl01). Together with AADFs, these allow users to see both how busy roads are within an area and the overall size of the road network.", "code": "Motor vehicle flow", "dataset": "motor-vehicle-flow", "canBeNegative": false, "periodFormat": "year", "frequency": "annual", "periodDomain": ["1993-01-01/P1Y", "2025-01-01/P1Y"], "hasTimeseries": true, "confidenceIntervals": false, "valueDomain": [100.0, 10200.0], "measure": "Annual average daily flow", "unit": "Annual average daily flow", "isMultivariate": false}]}}